==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Maglev Cat''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Bullet Train Cat''' when obtained from [[Revenge of Carnage (Merciless)|Revenge of Carnage]] and is level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Express Cat is basically a glass cannon, somewhat similar to [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|A. Bahamut]], [[Sanada Yukimura (Uber Rare Cat)|Yukimura]] and [[Swimmer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Swimmer Cat]] among others. With its super speed and strong attacks, it can be used to drill through clusters of enemies or deliver strong hits to a tough boss in-between attack frames. The [[Money Up]] ability is just a bonus that can be exploited against a peon that drops a lot of cash such as [[Doge Dark]] or [[B.B.Bunny]].

Express Cat has a long attack cycle and only 1 knockback, mean that it will usually only get in one attack before death, so think carefully about when to send it out. It is recommended to use it just after a boss enemy attacks, so it might even get in two or three attacks instead of being killed on the route to the boss. Using it against enemies with [[Knockback|knockback]] or [[Warp]], such as [[Shibalien Elite]] or [[Trolly Blogger]], is also a solution for getting it to attack again, provided if Express Cat does not die to the attack. Similarly, it may also be of use against weaker [[Assassin Bear|Assassin Bears]] as it can potentially tank long enough to reach and kill it. 

A great way of using Express Cat is stalling. Due to its long attack rate and workable health, it will remain in the same spot while also collecting double the cash from each peon, making it easier to get your worker cat to MAX.

Another good way of taking advantage of its Money Up ability is by chipping down a big enemy, such as [[Duche]], and sending out Express Cat to deliver the final blow, doubling the already high money drop, or by sending it out against a large group of Trolly Bloggers, who deal low damage with their knockback-inflicting attacks and reset its attack animation to generate huge amounts of money, such as in [[No Plan A (Deadly)|No Plan A]].

==='''True Form'''===
Bullet Train Cat gains some stat boosts and extra speed. Although the increase to health and attack seem minor, this makes it much better at dealing chip damage, which is its main use. Furthermore, its increased speed turns it into the fastest non-collab cat in the game, which is definitely worth something and makes it easier to time. Overall, worth the trouble of beating [[River Acheron]].

